    [Test][BugFix] Stabilize DeepSeek V4.1 MRV2 PCP nightly startup (#19477)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    The `DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-w8a8-PD-MRV2` nightly can fail during Prefill
    startup because the 1M-context KV cache requires about 5.56 GiB per rank
    while only about 5.07 GiB remains after model profiling.
    
    Root cause: #19243 reverted the PCP-local profile token-budget
    optimization. Each PCP rank therefore profiles the full token budget,
    increasing profile-stage memory use and leaving insufficient capacity
    for the KV cache.
    
    This patch keeps `--max-model-len 1048576` and changes only the Prefill
    configuration:
    
    - reduces `--max-num-batched-tokens` from `16384` to `8192` to lower
    profiling and per-iteration activation memory;
    - raises `--gpu-memory-utilization` from `0.9` to `0.92` to provide
    additional KV-cache capacity.
    
    The Decode configuration remains unchanged (`--max-num-batched-tokens
    400`, `--gpu-memory-utilization 0.95`). Lowering the Prefill batch-token
    cap may reduce the maximum Prefill batching capacity, so the existing
    nightly performance cases still need to be checked on NPU hardware.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. This changes an internal nightly test configuration only, so no
    release note fragment is needed.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Parsed the changed YAML with PyYAML.
    - Asserted the effective values after parsing:
    - Prefill: `max_model_len=1048576`, `max_num_batched_tokens=8192`,
    `gpu_memory_utilization=0.92`.
    - Decode: `max_model_len=1048576`, `max_num_batched_tokens=400`,
    `gpu_memory_utilization=0.95`.
    - `git diff --check` passed.
    - `bash format.sh ci` could not start locally because `pre-commit` is
    not installed in the host environment; repository CI is expected to run
    the required formatting checks.
    - The full two-node A3 nightly run is pending and is required before
    merge to verify startup, accuracy, and performance.
    
